messages:
jen: Quick check — creating a short onboarding blurb for the Node SDK that covers ESM vs CJS + bundlers (Next/Vite) + edge runtimes + auth. Wanted to capture the pragmatic defaults we recommend so customers don't get stuck. Any quick notes or gotchas?

omar: love this. high-level: default to providing both CJS and ESM entrypoints via exports, include a browser/edge-friendly build, and call out env vs header patterns for auth.

tyler: +1. also call out that Vite often bundles node builtins unless you mark them external. mention "browser" field and exports conditions.

mia: small thing — warn about top-level fs or crypto imports breaking in edge. recommend dynamic import guarded by isNode checks.

jen: example package.json snippet i'm going to include: 
```
{
  "name": "@redwood/node-sdk",
  "type": "module",
  "exports": {
    ".": {
      "import": "./dist/index.mjs",
      "require": "./dist/index.cjs",
      "browser": "./dist/index.browser.mjs"
    }
  }
}
```
jen: is that OK to suggest?

omar: looks good. maybe change top-level "type" to omit if you want CJS consumers to still default; but exports keys handle it. add a separate entry on interoperability (how to import in CJS consumers).

tyler: for Next/Vite notes:
- Next server runtime (node): use the regular node build (import/require ok)
- Next edge runtime (middleware/edge API): require the browser/edge build and avoid native modules
- Vite: add `optimizeDeps.exclude` for large CJS-only deps and mark native modules as external in ssr config

mia: auth pattern suggestion: for hosted -> env var (server), for edge -> require passing Authorization header from client (or use signed ephemeral tokens). doc snippet: `fetch('/api/edge-proxy', { headers: { Authorization: 'Bearer ' + token } })`

jen: streaming note — customers on edge often expect Response.body streaming. include small example for Node vs Edge:
```
// Node (sdk returns node stream)
const res = await client.stream(...)
for await (const chunk of res) { /* handle chunk */ }
// Edge (web ReadableStream)
const r = await client.stream(...)
const reader = r.getReader()
while (true) {
  const { done, value } = await reader.read()
  if (done) break
  // handle value (Uint8Array)
}
```

omar: good call. also mention encoding gotchas (TextDecoder + concat across chunks).

tyler: retries: surface that edge runtimes have different retry semantics (no true TCP-level reconnect). recommend idempotency keys and small client-side backoff.

jen: CI bot — i'll open a tiny docs PR with these bullets + code examples. can someone glance at wording? @tyler @omar @mia :eyes:

ci-bot: docs/pr-6423 opened by jen — https://github.com/redwood-inference/docs/pull/6423

omar: will review by EOD, i can suggest a tiny clarification on package.json wording.

tyler: will check streaming examples for clarity. small nit: use `TextDecoder` example for chunk decoding.

mia: thumbs up, will add an example for guarding native modules.

jen: awesome, thanks team — i'll fold feedback and merge once CI green. :sparkles:
